abstract: "A six-month snapshot of 615,200 pull requests from 148,801 outside contributors to 11,000 GitHub projects. Each project is ranked by what happens to a stranger's pull request: whether a human replies, reviews or merges it, and how soon."
keywords:
  - open source
  - pull requests
  - maintainer responsiveness
  - first contribution
